'''Arenaria''' (ar-ẹ̄-nā′ri-ä), ''n.'' [NL., fem. sing. of L. ''arenarius'', ''harenarius'': see ''arenarious''.] '''1.''' In ''ornith.'': (''a'') [''l. c.''] A disused specific name of several shore-birds or limicoline species of ''Scolopacidæ'', as the redshank, ''Totanus calidris''. (''b'') A generic name of the turnstone, ''Strepsilas interpres''. ''Brisson'', 1760. (''c'') A generic name of the sanderling, ''Calidris arenaria''. ''Meyer'', 1810. (''d'') [''l. c.''] The specific name of the same. ''Linnæus'', 1758, and most modern writers.—'''2.''' A genus of bivalve mollusks, of the family ''Tellinidæ'': synonymous with ''Scrobicularia''. ''Mühlfeld'', 1811.—'''3.''' In ''bot.'', an unimportant genus of low herbs, of the natural order ''Caryophyllaceæ'', allied to the chickweeds; the sandworts.

